  "title": "Linear – The system for product development",
  "visibleTextExcerpt": "Skip to content →\nLog in\nSign up\nThe product development system for teams and agents\nThe product development system for teams and agents\n\nPurpose-built for planning and building products. Designed for the AI era.\n\nNew\nLoops →\nLinear\nPulse\nInbox\nMy issues\nReviews\nWorkspace\nInitiatives\nProjects\nMore\nFavorites\nFaster app launch\nAgent tasks\nAgent Insights\nUI Refresh\nDRV-8852\nFaster app launch\n1 / 84\nFaster app launch\n\nRender UI before vehicle_state sync when minimum required state is present, instead of blocking on full refresh during iOS startup.\n\nActivity\nLinear created the issue via Slack on behalf of Karri\n·\n2min ago\nTriage Intelligence added the labels Performance and iOS\n·\n2min ago\nkarri\n·\n4 min ago\nRight now we show a spinner forever, which makes it look like the car disappeared...\njori\n·\njust now\n@Linear can you take a stab at this?\nLinear\nconnected by Jori\n·\n2 min ago\nChanged 2 files\nDraft PR awaiting your review\n·\n2 min ago\nLinear moved from Todo to In Progress\n·\njust now\nLinear\nOpus 5\n\nFix the dimmed ride rows that never reset and open a PR\n\nDRV-364\nadded to context\nWorked for 10 sec\n\nPushed and opened a draft PR. Removed dimmedIds — isItemDimmed now checks waitingStatusById directly.\n\nChanged\n2 files\n+22\n−10\nDraft\nReset dimmed ride rows\nmaster\n←\nride/drv-364-reset-dimmed-rows\nPreview\n\nReply…\n\nSkills\nReviews\nRevert\nProperties\nIn Progress\nMedium\nKarri\nLinear\nCycle 144\nLabels\nPerformance\niOS\nReleases\nLinear App\n1.6881...\n⋅\nJun 25\n\nPOWERING THE COMPANIES BUILDING THE FUTURE\n\nA new species of product tool. Purpose-built for modern teams with AI workflows at its core, Lin",
